<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut by high winds.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut by high winds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Russian oil outlet Novorossiisk was closed on Wednesday because of high winds and swell, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea terminal closed at 2150 local time.</p>
<p>The biggest berth at Novorossiisk has been closed since December 9 for repairs and is not expected to reopen for another week.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea oil export terminals at Odessa and Tuapse were operating normally on Wednesday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>Russia's outlet on the Baltic, Latvian Ventspils, also was open.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 1542 8060</p>
